## Architecture and editing rules

- `CreativeDirector/AGENT.md`: full V1 orchestrator/critic definition.
- `BriefMachine/AGENT.md`, `DesignChamp/AGENT.md`, `WordSmither/AGENT.md`: the constitution describes these as placeholders to design separately. Inspect their actual content before extending them.
- `.claude/agents/`: thin wrappers named `brief-machine`, `creative-engine-director`, `design-champ`, and `word-smither`. Keep role detail in the corresponding `AGENT.md`.
- `.claude/skills/`: discovery location for approved skills; currently the inspected directory contains a README. Department `skills/` folders organize ownership/evaluation. Do not install third-party skills without the review and user approval required by `CLAUDE.md`.
- Active framework registry lives in `CLAUDE.md`: creative object taxonomy, creative trajectory evaluation, Hey Whipple copycraft, brief normalization, creative direction audit, and optional education enrollment intake. Frameworks are additive and selectively applied; do not replace older methods simply because a newer one exists.
- Modes: EXPLORE, DEVELOP, JUDGE. Canonical verdicts: KILL, REWORK, ADVANCE, BET THE PITCH. Do not impose judgment gates on rough exploration.
- Global method stays in role directories and `shared/`. Client facts stay within their own `projects/<client>/` boundary. Do not read other clients' work as evidence for the current assignment.
- Raw sources are immutable. Normalize before creative work; retain provenance, unresolved conflicts, claim status, and older reviewed versions. Project findings require deliberate user confirmation before promotion to client knowledge.
- `normalized-brief.md` is the project briefing authority; the project README is an index/summary. Use versioned working files and preserve reviewed versions.
- Root `briefs/` and `outputs/` are superseded by client workspaces.

